---
import SocialLinks from '@ui/SocialLinks.astro';
import { site } from '@/config';

const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<footer class="mt-8 border-t border-(--color-border)">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-8">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
      <span class="text-sm text-(--color-text-muted)">&copy; {year} {site.name}</span>
      <SocialLinks trace="footer" />
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xs leading-relaxed text-(--color-text-muted)">
      This site runs self-hosted analytics on my homelab, with no third-party trackers and no
      advertising. The data stays on my own hardware. A long-lived first-party cookie identifies
      returning visitors. Each visit records your IP address, the approximate location and ISP
      derived from it, browser and device details, and on-page behavior: clicks, hovers, time per
      section, and an aggregate summary of pointer motion used to tell humans from bots (raw
      coordinates never leave the page). If your browser sends Global Privacy Control, the visit is
      still recorded, but the public dashboard only ever counts it toward the totals, never shows
      it. The dashboard is
      <a href="https://trace.tsilenz.io" data-trace-event="footer-trace-live">public to browse</a>,
      with identifying fields masked.
    </p>
  </div>
</footer>
